1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:09,680
The one I offered

2
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:16,120
Special Investigations Chief,
you've got a big topknot.

3
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:19,200
I've got no grudge against you,

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,320
but you're going to be asleep for a while.

5
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,520
W-what?

6
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,760
Hahahahaha!

7
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,800
Toh!

8
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,860
Tah!

9
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,620
Wah!

10
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,980
Yah!

11
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,040
Yah!

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:41,190
Whoa,

13
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:47,540
I'm gonna leak, I'm gonna leak!

14
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:55,240
Detective?

15
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,720
Who's there?

16
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:11,260
Who the hell are you?

17
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,680
Open!

18
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:16,240
Mustang Detective, prepare yourself! Rocket!

19
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,680
Now there's nobody left to get in the way.

20
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:33,080
Get up, you Sanbagarasu of the
Special Investigation Division!

21
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:35,640
I'll get my revenge, mark my words.

22
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:45,140
Die Hard 2: The Lowest Battle on Earth

23
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,500
Autumn is here,
when the sky is high and horses grow fat

24
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:59,100
You two need to grow up fast too, okay?

25
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,580
Chief.

26
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:03,720
Good morning.

27
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,420
Morning.

28
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,100
A cactus!

29
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,580
You've started growing cacti too?

30
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:12,840
Yeah, Hiromi gave it to me for my birthday.

31
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,880
A present from your daughter?

32
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,040
Well, yeah.

33
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,540
What's this smell?

34
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:22,900
Just as expected, Chief.
The flowers really make a difference.

35
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,640
This is matsutake, isn't it!

36
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,440
These are crabs.

37
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:29,700
What?

38
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:33,320
Wow! Hairy crabs and matsutake mushrooms!

39
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,780
Where did you get so many?

40
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:40,140
My dad sent them, but I can't eat
them all by myself, so I'm sharing.

41
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,100
Mine were gifts too.

42
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,740
I thought they'd taste better
if we all ate them together.

43
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:48,240
You two are really good guys.

44
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,960
I'm happy to have such good friends.

45
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:56,920
Payday's still away,
and we haven't eaten anything decent lately.

46
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,380
Let's all eat once our shift is over.

47
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,160
Then let's make it a hotpot.

48
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,080
Hotpot

49
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:06,440
Matsutake and hairy crab hotpot?
That's a real luxury.

50
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:09,980
Let's invite Honda and Maria
too and throw a big hotpot party!

51
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,320
Sounds great.

52
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,980
Then it's settled.
I'll run and let them know.

53
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:16,500
Hey, Ryotsu!

54
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:20,060
Honestly, he only gets this excited
when there's something like this.

55
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,520
Is this about right for
the matsutake and crab?

56
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,660
But that's a huge amount!

57
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:31,140
Tonight we're gonna eat and eat and eat!

58
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,020
I bought some napa cabbage and green onions.

59
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,380
I got tofu and shirataki.

60
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:39,660
I brought kelp and chicken.

61
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,440
I borrowed a pot, a chicken platter,
and ponzu from the dorm.

62
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:44,900
You borrowed them?

63
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:48,340
Honestly, it's like wrestling
sumo in someone else's ring!

64
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,720
Sorry, it's right before payday.

65
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,060
Fine, I guess it can't be helped.

66
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:55,240
Then boil water in that pot
and make dashi with the kelp.

67
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,000
Okay!

68
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,040
By the way, Ryotsu.

69
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,980
What did you bring?

70
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,120
Me? I didn't really -

71
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,420
Idiot!

72
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:06,280
After all that talk to Honda,
what kind of contribution is this?

73
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:09,000
I'm an officer at this police box too,

74
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,700
and anyone who brings nothing
doesn't get to join the hotpot.

75
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:13,600
N-no way! That's cruel!

76
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,500
I skipped lunch and was
looking forward to this!

77
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:19,280
If you want to eat,
bring any ingredients you like.

78
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,980
Fine, I'll bring something!
I'll bring something!

79
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:28,520
That said, I don't have any money.

80
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,880
Pachinko balls

81
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,480
Right, I don't need money.
With this one shot -

82
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,120
Yes!

83
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:49,780
From a single pachinko ball, in just 30
minutes, I'll win this many prizes. Me!

84
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:55,812
It's a cactus.

85
00:04:55,862 --> 00:04:59,100
There are no greens at all,
so I'll take this.

86
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,392
It's a frog.

87
00:05:03,442 --> 00:05:05,740
I'll take this one while I'm at it.

88
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,160
Ryotsu's taking his time.

89
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:14,360
Sorry to keep you waiting.

90
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:17,000
Ryotsu,
you did bring the ingredients, right?

91
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,340
Yeah, of course. Here you go, see?

92
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,800
W-what is that?

93
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:25,080
It's a prize I won at pachinko.

94
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:28,420
No, I mean that thing sticking out there.

95
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,080
It's a frog.

96
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,820
This is exactly why you're a problem,
young lady.

97
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:37,700
Frogs are on the menu at izakayas, you know.

98
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:40,000
What are you doing?

99
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:40,920
It's a dark hotpot.

100
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,400
Dark hotpot?

101
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:46,940
I've put in my share, so I'm joining in.

102
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:49,020
You put the frog in too?

103
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:53,440
You said anything goes as long as it's a hotpot ingredient,
Chief, didn't you?

104
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:55,460
I did say that.

105
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:57,220
Then there's no problem, is there?

106
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,840
You didn't put anything weird in there too,
did you?

107
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,720
It's a pachinko prize,
so it's perfectly edible.

108
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:04,760
But...

109
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:08,140
Come on, eat up!
The dark hotpot party has begun!

110
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,820
Well, there's no choice.

111
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,160
Then let's eat in turn.

112
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,720
Maria goes first.

113
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:14,900
Yes.

114
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:21,980
The rule of dark hotpot is that once
you've touched an item with your chopsticks,

115
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,800
you absolutely have to eat it.

116
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:24,980
Understood.

117
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,480
It's sweet and delicious.

118
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,440
I didn't put anything sweet in there!

119
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:36,500
Then that must be the
canned pineapple I put in.

120
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,840
I'm glad.

121
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:39,380
Alright, next is Nakagawa.

122
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:40,540
Y-yes.

123
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:49,920
This is matsutake! Delicious.

124
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,700
Reiko, you're the best!

125
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,520
I'm glad, Kei-chan.

126
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:55,460
Hey, that's a slippery one!

127
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,540
Alright, my turn next.

128
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,180
That's a frog, isn't it!

129
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,460
Why do I have to be the one who eats it?

130
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,540
It's because your conduct has
been bad lately that this happens.

131
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:09,820
Eat it properly, it's the rule after all.

132
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,080
I know.

133
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:15,180
Alright, is it my turn next?

134
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:19,780
Ouch!

135
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:21,920
That's going to cause an injury, isn't it?

136
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,680
Looks like it.

137
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,620
Unlike fishermen,
I've always behaved well, so

138
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:32,320
For a hairy crab, it feels kind of squishy.

139
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:33,820
What is this?

140
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:36,560
No, Chief, you have to eat it properly.

141
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,420
It seems to be some kind of vegetable.

142
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,720
That's not a vegetable, you know.

143
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,320
Hey, turn on the light.

144
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:44,340
Right.

145
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,620
T-this is a cactus!

146
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,240
I'm the one who put it in.

147
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,700
Is there such a thing as
an expense for pachinko?

148
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,520
No, I picked it up from over there.

149
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,600
Ryo-chan,
wasn't this in front of the police box...?

150
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,200
Yeah.

151
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,840
This is bad, senpai.

152
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:10,120
Bad? In Mexico,
cactus is a proper food, you know.

153
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,360
That's not what I meant...

154
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,760
Nakagawa, forget it.

155
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:19,060
Ryotsu! How dare you put my
precious cactus in the hotpot!

156
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,420
Don't tell me this cactus is...

157
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:26,280
the cactus Hiromi gave me! Eeeeeeh!

158
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:31,520
Sorry, Chief, we had no idea at all!

159
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:32,540
Chief?

160
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:44,960
You idiot!
I've really had it with you today!

161
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,320
You're fired, got it?

162
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,860
So what if I put a cactus in the hotpot?

163
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:55,500
Are you really putting a cactus before a
subordinate you've worked with for years?

164
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,080
That's right.

165
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,020
Oh my.

166
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:02,880
Fine, I get it.

167
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:07,280
I've had enough of working
under a boss like you, too!

168
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,920
I quit, effective today!

169
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:09,320
What?

170
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:10,540
No way...

171
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:20,920
Ryo-chan

172
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:21,620
Senpai

173
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,300
Ryo-chan

174
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:24,880
Ryo-chan

175
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:27,680
The Chief regrets that he went too far, too.

176
00:09:28,020 --> 00:09:31,560
He says he'll withdraw your
resignation if you bow your head.

177
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:32,460
So,

178
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:33,960
It's too late now.

179
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:36,240
Senpai, don't be so stubborn about it.

180
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:39,600
A boss who loves his cactus more than his noisy subordinate?
Who needs him?

181
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,560
The feeling's mutual.
I'm glad to be rid of you!

182
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,300
Ryo-chan...

183
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:47,200
Take away the police officer from Ryo-chan,
and what on earth is left?

184
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:47,840
What?

185
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,185
Ryo-sama,

186
00:09:50,235 --> 00:09:53,960
if Ryo-sama is going to become a bride,
then I'll quit the police too.

187
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,900
Maria, I appreciate the sentiment,
but this is my problem.

188
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:03,520
Either way, starting today,
I'm done with the police box.

189
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,080
Take care, everyone.

190
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:08,780
Ryo-san, Ryo-chan...

191
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:10,340
Senpai, Ryo-san...

192
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,300
Aaaaaah!

193
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:31,000
Take the police officer out of both of them,
and what on earth is left?

194
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:36,740
Aaaaah... this is -

195
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:41,480
Aaaaaaah!

196
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,420
Arira arira laaaa!

197
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,350
I am the captain of the Water Police,

198
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,240
Umino Dozaemon!

199
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:02,400
Dolphin, whose trademark is
his charming Yashioki cut!

200
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,140
I should've known it was you.

201
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:08,760
Long time no see, Ryotsu.

202
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:11,540
You still take forever
to make your entrance!

203
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,760
By the way, what are you doing out here?

204
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,540
I heard you got fired from
the Kameari Park police box.

205
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:20,140
News travels fast.

206
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,820
You don't have anywhere to stay, do you?

207
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,560
Well, no.

208
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:27,320
Then you should come to the Special
Criminal Investigation Division.

209
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:30,220
To the Special Criminal
Investigation Division.

210
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:41,140
You guys actually live in a place like this?

211
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:43,280
It's like a hotel!

212
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:45,440
The dormitory takes up
the fifth floor and above.

213
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:46,360
Dormitory?

214
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:48,780
How many people are in the Special
Criminal Investigation Division?

215
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,380
Right now, there are six of us.

216
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,920
Just six of you live here?

217
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:56,980
This way is the rock bath.

218
00:11:56,980 --> 00:12:00,180
And this is the sauna.

219
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:01,340
You even have a sauna?

220
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:04,560
There's also a game
center and a karaoke room.

221
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,200
That's right, it's not on this floor,
but there's a movie theater too.

222
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,360
What a huge difference
from the Nikoniko Dormitory.

223
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:14,040
We in the Special Criminal Investigation Division are the elite of the elite,
you know.

224
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:23,200
They don't look very elite, though.

225
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,380
This is the training room.

226
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:29,840
Kaipan Deka and Gekkō Deka should be here.

227
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,140
Clang!

228
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:37,520
Whaaaaat?

229
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:51,000
Unlike those other bulge-showing cops, whenever a case comes up, they solve everything in just their swim trunks.
One of the Special Criminal Investigation Division's Sambagarasu.

230
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:55,060
Ohh, I'm home!

231
00:12:55,060 --> 00:13:01,760
Long time no see.
Why are you using the door?

232
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:05,280
What?

233
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:07,400
W-what's this music?

234
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,260
Moonlight Power!

235
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:11,020
Oh no, not them again.

236
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:20,040
Pick up!

237
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,680
Venus Deka, you're too early!

238
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,040
S-sorry. It was the short version.

239
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,540
Allow me to explain.

240
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,880
By changing costumes,
Moonlight Deka

241
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,820
can unleash seven special powers!

242
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:41,920
Then, I...

243
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:50,040
Moonlight is my energy!

244
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:52,520
Messenger from the Moon, Moonlight Deka!

245
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:54,560
Likewise, Venus Deka!

246
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,340
Kenzan, reporting in!

247
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,340
Why can't you two just
make a normal entrance?

248
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:02,200
I'm going home after all.

249
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:03,320
Wait!

250
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,020
I really need your help.

251
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:09,220
Let go! Getting involved
with you lot never ends well.

252
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,500
The Special Criminal Investigation
Division is being targeted.

253
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:14,640
Tiger Deka and Mustang
Deka have already been hit,

254
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,900
and even the chief, Chonmage Deka,

255
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:20,200
were seriously injured by
someone and are in the hospital.

256
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:23,480
Then all the more reason I
can't stay in a place like this!

257
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,680
So you'll help us, then?

258
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:28,140
As expected of you, Ryotsu-kun.

259
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:30,300
I knew you'd say that.

260
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,800
I never said that!

261
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,760
Are you two even listening to me?

262
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:34,940
Let's go.

263
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:38,120
Then bow your head to Chief Ohara

264
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,380
and go back to the police box?

265
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:41,420
I can't do that!

266
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,920
Then join the Special Criminal
Investigation Division.

267
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,720
We'd welcome you.

268
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,080
Fine, I understand.

269
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:50,100
I'll impose on you for a while.

270
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:50,780
I see.

271
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:53,860
Since you'll have your
moving boxes to unpack today,

272
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:56,040
let's leave the greeting
to the Chief for tomorrow.

273
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:58,600
The Chief, Chonmage Deka,

274
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,000
isn't he in the hospital?

275
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,280
The chief has been replaced by a new one.

276
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,840
Did some career officer
come over from headquarters?

277
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,880
No, he was promoted
from within our division.

278
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,280
He has a 100% criminal arrest rate.

279
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:17,100
That guy set a milestone that neither I, Dolphin
Deka, nor Moonlight Deka could ever achieve.

280
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,340
Who is this guy?

281
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,660
You know him well.

282
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,660
Someone I know well too.

283
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:29,420
I see.

284
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:30,680
Good morning, everyone.

285
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,320
Good morning.

286
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:37,820
What? Ryotsu's late again? That idiot!

287
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,460
Um...

288
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:53,800
Chief, please forgive Ryo-chan
and let him work here again.

289
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,340
I'm asking you too.

290
00:15:56,420 --> 00:16:00,540
What are you talking about? With him gone,
it's so peaceful. Isn't that better?

291
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:04,260
This is how a police box should really be.

292
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:07,960
Hahahahaha!

293
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,100
Good morning.

294
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,340
Section Chief,
I've brought Senior Patrol Officer Ryotsu.

295
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:24,700
The Section Chief says,
"Thank you for your hard work."

296
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,540
It's Dolphin!

297
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:34,640
He says not to address him so casually.

298
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:38,240
What? Hey, what's going on here?

299
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,260
It's your fault, you know.

300
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:44,260
Back when you worked as Hato Poppo Deka in
the Special Criminal Investigation Division,

301
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,121
you know,

302
00:16:46,171 --> 00:16:49,580
you had dozens of
pigeons spy on Chief Ohara,

303
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:52,560
and made people collect loose money off the ground,
didn't you?

304
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:54,700
Well, yeah.

305
00:16:54,700 --> 00:17:00,020
Section Chief Eibun used the
information-gathering techniques you taught him

306
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,693
to take control of hundreds of thousands

307
00:17:01,743 --> 00:17:05,000
of pigeons across the city, millions
of them, with a rich source of funds,

308
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:10,640
turning them into his subordinates and building an
information network more powerful than the police.

309
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:12,720
Because of that,

310
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,740
Pictacrin! Somebody catch them!

311
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,440
solving any crime on the spot,

312
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:43,440
the Special Criminal Investigation Division
became the detectives with the highest arrest rate.

313
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,780
In recognition of that achievement,

314
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:49,020
Topknot even took over from
Kani and became section chief.

315
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:49,820
What?!

316
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:55,620
now he even has a gorgeous
secretary who understands pigeons.

317
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:57,760
He's living a life of leisure and comfort.

318
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:00,100
Wow, that's amazing, Denemon.

319
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:02,340
It's practically thanks
to me that he got promoted.

320
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,340
The Chief says not to make it
easy for people to come here.

321
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:10,240
How dare you, a pigeon!

322
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,240
Stop it, Ryotsu!

323
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:18,800
Ow ow ow ow

324
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,780
Stop it, you idiot! Ow! Stop, stop!

325
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:26,140
The Chief says he won't
tolerate any disrespect.

326
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,560
Stop it! Please, stop!

327
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:36,260
You guys, letting that pigeon lord it over you like that,
doesn't it make you furious?

328
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:38,580
Even if he's a pigeon, the section
chief is still the section chief.

329
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:42,640
We may be Special Criminal Investigators, but
we're still salaried men working for someone else.

330
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:46,140
Well, well, aren't you awfully
understanding all of a sudden.

331
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,020
Ryo-san!

332
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:50,620
W-what is it?

333
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,300
The Chief sent this.

334
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:53,700
What's this?

335
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:56,840
They're taking you on as
Hato Poppo's apprentice,

336
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,300
so you're to wear this on your head,
he says.

337
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:01,180
What kind of joke is this?

338
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:03,720
Who the hell can work under some pigeon!

339
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:04,980
Ryotsu!

340
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:07,100
Let go, Dolphin, you oaf!

341
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:09,840
If I upset Section Chief Denemon here,

342
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:11,300
I won't be able to stay here anymore!

343
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,960
I have to grin and bear it.

344
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:17,780
That's fine.

345
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,720
Damn you, Denemon!

346
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,060
Just wait and see what
happens when you anger me.

347
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:25,080
I'll make you regret this!

348
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:22,280
Become one.

349
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,300
I am the champion! Rocket!

350
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,700
Aaaaah!

351
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:35,360
Well done, well done.

352
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:42,880
Your strength is far superior to Trunks Deka,
Dolphin, and Moonlight Deka.

353
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:50,720
I haven't forgotten the grudge of being defeated by that pervert
bastard's freak technique and locked up in prison for five years.

354
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:53,080
Me too.

355
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:57,300
To take revenge on that Dolphin bastard and his dolphins,
I trained sharks.

356
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,700
Me too.

357
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:03,720
To defeat Moonlight Deka, I came up
with this transformation technique.

358
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,200
What a reliable bunch.

359
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:12,660
Right now I'm figuring out how to lure those
three detectives in and take them all out at once.

360
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:16,520
Until then,
keep those flames of revenge burning.

361
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:23,200
Emergency! Emergency!

362
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:26,240
Special Criminal Investigation Division,
please gather in the operations room.

363
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:32,520
Hato Poppo, no godly name...
Ryotsu Kankichi, reporting for duty!

364
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:40,880
A pistol robber has taken hostages at
a finance company and is holed up inside.

365
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:44,820
Just now, a dispatch request came in for
the Special Criminal Investigation Division.

366
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:55,860
Wow, they've really rigged this up.

367
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:00,680
So high-tech.

368
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,180
This is the culprit.

369
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:05,680
The suspect is barricaded on
the fifth floor of this building.

370
00:22:06,780 --> 00:22:07,720
There's a river

371
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,840
I'll go.

372
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:11,560
No, if it's the fifth floor,
we can get in from the sky.

373
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,340
Leave it to us.

374
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:15,220
This is a case for the ground.

375
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:16,700
My time to shine.

376
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:26,060
The Section Chief said that as long as we
have Gekkō Deka and Hato Poppo Deka apprentice,

377
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:28,760
the case will be solved easily.

378
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:33,620
Apprentice Pote Deka.

379
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:34,700
Let's go.

380
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:45,920
Hey, you!

381
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,580
Why am I always stuck here?

382
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:50,420
Idiot!

383
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:51,620
What are you babbling about?

384
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,400
The trainee says that's good enough for him.

385
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:57,420
You only said one thing,
but that's a pretty long interpretation.

386
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:07,500
Hey, don't stall,
just put the money in already!

387
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:11,760
Get up and go!

388
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:15,360
What?

389
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:25,260
Are you trying to hit the jackpot,
you idiot?

390
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:29,080
It's charging straight at us!

391
00:23:30,340 --> 00:23:31,300
Cut it loose!

392
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,000
Eeeeeeh!

393
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,180
Aaaaaaah!

394
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:40,920
Eeeeeeh!

395
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,500
Eeeeeeh!

396
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:44,100
Eeeeeeh!

397
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:45,280
Eeeeeeh!

398
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:46,620
Eeeeeeh!

399
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:47,420
Eeeeeeh!

400
00:23:47,420 --> 00:23:48,180
Eeeeeeh!

401
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:49,760
We did it!

402
00:24:00,580 --> 00:24:02,740
Using Ryotsu as a sacrificial pawn!

403
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:04,980
Section Chief Rengemon is truly terrifying.

